WEBVTT

00:00:37.358 --> 00:00:39.377
Dad's missing I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:40.605
I can't do this alone.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.046
Dad's giving us a job to do.

00:00:42.081 --> 00:00:44.071
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:46.027
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:46.062 --> 00:00:49.020
This Demon killed mom and
Jess. I got to find dad.

00:00:49.055 --> 00:00:50.768
I've got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:50.803 --> 00:00:51.601
I'm Meg.

00:00:51.636 --> 00:00:52.628
So, where are you headed?

00:00:52.663 --> 00:00:53.620
No way I'm telling you.

00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:55.985
You could be some freak.

00:00:56.532 --> 00:00:57.805
Dad.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.764
<i>ust to get a glimpse
beyond this illusion</i>

00:01:01.799 --> 00:01:02.981
<i>I was soaring ever</i>

00:01:03.016 --> 00:01:05.857
1835, Samuel Colt made a special gun.

00:01:05.892 --> 00:01:08.698
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:13.422
<i>Though my eyes could see
I still was a blind man</i>

00:01:13.457 --> 00:01:17.108
<i>Though my mind could
think I still was a mad man</i>

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.881
<i>I hear the voices when I'm dreaming</i>

00:01:19.916 --> 00:01:23.244
I have nightmares. And
sometime they come true.

00:01:25.106 --> 00:01:28.502
<i>Carry on my wayward son</i>

00:01:28.537 --> 00:01:30.497
<i>There'll be peace when you are</i>

00:01:30.532 --> 00:01:33.668
You two are all I've got. But I
guess we are stronger as a family.

00:01:33.703 --> 00:01:35.642
We go after this thing, together.

00:01:35.677 --> 00:01:36.145
Yes, sir.

00:01:36.146 --> 00:01:38.703
<i>Don't you cry no more</i>

00:02:03.641 --> 00:02:04.920
Good morning.

00:02:05.611 --> 00:02:07.274
Can I help you?

00:02:08.413 --> 00:02:10.390
I kind of...

00:02:10.425 --> 00:02:12.367
I need to talk.

00:02:14.115 --> 00:02:16.363
That's what I'm here for.

00:02:18.809 --> 00:02:21.431
I've done some things.

00:02:22.664 --> 00:02:24.330
Not good things.

00:02:24.365 --> 00:02:27.169
Well, there's always
forgiveness for us who seek it.

00:02:27.204 --> 00:02:29.351
For everyone?

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.661
Are you sure?

00:02:31.696 --> 00:02:33.409
I'll like to say...

00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:36.911
Salvation was created for sinners.

00:02:38.348 --> 00:02:41.402
Tell me what's on your mind.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.081
Well, I've lied a lot.

00:02:46.116 --> 00:02:48.156
I've Stolen.

00:02:48.191 --> 00:02:50.161
I've lusted...

00:02:50.196 --> 00:02:53.001
And the other day I met this man.

00:02:53.036 --> 00:02:56.744
A nice guy, you know?

00:02:57.465 --> 00:03:03.448
We had a really good
chat. Sort of like this.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:10.237
And I slit his throat and ripped
his heart out through his chest.

00:03:10.272 --> 00:03:12.281
Does that make me a bad person?

00:03:12.316 --> 00:03:13.837
I know what you are.

00:03:15.965 --> 00:03:18.268
You can't be here.

00:03:18.303 --> 00:03:20.025
This is hollowed ground.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.534
Please...

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:24.721
Maybe that works in the minor leagues.

00:03:24.756 --> 00:03:27.399
But not with me.

00:03:52.057 --> 00:03:54.655
You throw like a girl.

00:03:55.478 --> 00:03:57.698
What do you want?

00:03:58.146 --> 00:04:00.825
The Winchesters.

00:04:00.992 --> 00:04:04.431
I haven't spoken to John
Winchester for over a year.

00:04:04.466 --> 00:04:06.475
You're wasting you time.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.528
Even if I knew where they were

00:04:08.563 --> 00:04:10.947
I'd never tell you.

00:04:10.982 --> 00:04:13.072
I know.

00:05:03.777 --> 00:05:05.334
So, this is it?

00:05:05.369 --> 00:05:07.637
This is everything I know.

00:05:07.672 --> 00:05:10.569
Look, our whole lives we've been
searching for this demon right?

00:05:10.604 --> 00:05:12.962
Not a trace. Just nothing.

00:05:12.997 --> 00:05:15.286
Until about a year ago.

00:05:15.321 --> 00:05:17.452
For the first time I picked up a trail.

00:05:17.487 --> 00:05:18.649
That's when you took off.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:19.586
Yeah.

00:05:19.621 --> 00:05:23.354
The demon must have come
out of hiding or hibernation.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.567
All right, so what's
this trail you've found?

00:05:25.602 --> 00:05:29.067
Starts in Arizona. Then
New Jersey, California.

00:05:29.102 --> 00:05:31.423
House is burned down to the ground.

00:05:31.458 --> 00:05:34.110
It's going after families.

00:05:34.145 --> 00:05:35.696
Just like it went after us.

00:05:35.731 --> 00:05:37.115
Families with infants?

00:05:37.116 --> 00:05:38.136
Yeah.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:41.220
The night of the kid's
six month birthday.

00:05:41.655 --> 00:05:43.325
I was six months old that night?

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.965
Exactly six months.

00:05:45.019 --> 00:05:50.416
So, basically this demon is going
after these kids for some reason.

00:05:51.148 --> 00:05:53.852
Same way it came for me.

00:05:54.597 --> 00:05:57.587
So, mom's death?

00:05:57.874 --> 00:05:59.440
Jessica, it's all because of me?

00:05:59.475 --> 00:06:00.342
We don't know that Sam.

00:06:00.343 --> 00:06:01.955
Oh, really? Cause I say
we're pretty damn sure Dean.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:04.413
For the last time. What happened
to them is not your fault.

00:06:04.448 --> 00:06:06.837
Yeah, you're right. It's not
my fault. But it's my problem.

00:06:06.872 --> 00:06:08.837
No, it's not your
problem. It's our problem.

00:06:08.872 --> 00:06:12.908
Okay. That's enough.

00:06:18.068 --> 00:06:19.862
So, why is it doing it?

00:06:19.897 --> 00:06:20.948
What does it want?

00:06:20.983 --> 00:06:23.701
I wish I had more answers. I do.

00:06:23.736 --> 00:06:26.385
I've always been one step behind it.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:30.060
Look I've never got
there in time to save...

00:06:35.248 --> 00:06:38.479
So how do we find it?
Before it hits again?

00:06:38.679 --> 00:06:40.647
There' re signs.

00:06:40.682 --> 00:06:42.214
Look, it took me a
while to see the patterns

00:06:42.249 --> 00:06:47.135
but days before these fires
signs crop up in an area.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:52.022
Cattle deaths, temperature
fluctuations, electrical storms.

00:06:52.577 --> 00:06:55.581
And then we backed and checked...

00:06:55.616 --> 00:06:58.887
These things happened in Lawrence?

00:06:58.922 --> 00:07:02.158
A week before your mother died.

00:07:04.041 --> 00:07:06.987
And in Palo Alto.

00:07:08.881 --> 00:07:11.308
Before Jessica.

00:07:11.343 --> 00:07:15.702
And these signs they're starting again.

00:07:16.086 --> 00:07:18.194
Where?

00:07:18.332 --> 00:07:21.325
Salvation, Iowa.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.385
Damn it!

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:55.416
What is it?

00:07:55.451 --> 00:07:56.571
Son of a bitch!

00:07:56.606 --> 00:07:57.692
What is it?

00:07:58.145 --> 00:07:59.676
I just got a call from Caleb.

00:07:59.711 --> 00:08:00.962
Is he okay?

00:08:00.997 --> 00:08:04.198
He's fine. Jim Murphy's dead.

00:08:04.233 --> 00:08:06.291
Pastor Jim?

00:08:07.342 --> 00:08:09.343
How?

00:08:09.378 --> 00:08:11.442
Throat was slashed.

00:08:11.477 --> 00:08:14.157
He bled out.

00:08:16.989 --> 00:08:20.009
Caleb said they found traces
of sulfur at Jim's place.

00:08:20.044 --> 00:08:21.620
The Demon?

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:23.971
The Demon?

00:08:24.006 --> 00:08:26.978
I don't know. Could be. He just got...

00:08:27.013 --> 00:08:30.075
He got careless he slipped up.

00:08:30.868 --> 00:08:34.287
Maybe the Demon knows
we're getting close.

00:08:34.322 --> 00:08:35.518
What do you want to do?

00:08:35.553 --> 00:08:37.886
Now we act like every second counts.

00:08:37.921 --> 00:08:40.995
There's two hospitals and a
health center in this County.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:43.053
We split up, we cover more ground.

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:44.423
I want records.

00:08:44.458 --> 00:08:48.525
I want a list of every infant who's
gonna be six months old in the next week.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.521
Dad, that can be dozens of kids.

00:08:50.556 --> 00:08:52.410
How the hell are we gonna
know which one's the right one?

00:08:52.445 --> 00:08:55.051
We check them all. That's how.

00:08:55.543 --> 00:08:58.298
You got any better ideas?

00:08:59.822 --> 00:09:01.752
No, sir.

00:09:10.522 --> 00:09:11.939
Dad?

00:09:15.064 --> 00:09:17.123
Yeah.

00:09:18.667 --> 00:09:20.739
It's Jim.

00:09:21.113 --> 00:09:23.406
You know, I can't...

00:09:29.474 --> 00:09:31.638
This ends, now.

00:09:31.673 --> 00:09:33.767
I'm ending it.

00:09:33.802 --> 00:09:36.802
I don't care what it takes.

00:10:26.493 --> 00:10:27.704
Here you go, officer.

00:10:27.739 --> 00:10:28.853
Thank you.

00:10:44.957 --> 00:10:48.075
Hi, is there anything I can do for you?

00:10:48.434 --> 00:10:50.800
Oh, God, yes.

00:10:52.484 --> 00:10:55.092
Only I uh...

00:10:55.127 --> 00:10:58.044
Working right now, so...

00:11:48.237 --> 00:11:50.364
Train.

00:12:58.892 --> 00:13:00.175
Hi.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:04.015
Here, let me hold that. I don't
think you need that anymore.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.666
She's gorgeous, is she yours?

00:13:06.701 --> 00:13:07.333
Yeah.

00:13:07.368 --> 00:13:08.863
Oh, wow. Hi.

00:13:08.864 --> 00:13:11.832
I'm sorry, I'm Sam. I
just moved in up the block.

00:13:11.867 --> 00:13:13.291
Oh, hey. I'm Monica.

00:13:13.326 --> 00:13:13.760
Monica.

00:13:13.761 --> 00:13:14.684
This is Rosy.

00:13:14.719 --> 00:13:15.277
Rosy?

00:13:15.278 --> 00:13:17.702
Yeah. So, welcome to the neighborhood.

00:13:17.737 --> 00:13:19.242
Thank you.

00:13:19.277 --> 00:13:20.800
She's such a good baby.

00:13:20.835 --> 00:13:22.989
I know, she... I mean, she never cries.

00:13:23.024 --> 00:13:25.197
She just stares at everybody.

00:13:25.232 --> 00:13:27.336
Sometimes she looks at you and...

00:13:27.371 --> 00:13:30.206
I swear it's like
she's reading your mind.

00:13:30.414 --> 00:13:32.873
What about you Monica?
Have you lived here long?

00:13:32.908 --> 00:13:35.914
Oh, my husband and I we bought this
place just before Rosy was born.

00:13:35.949 --> 00:13:37.159
How old is Rosy?

00:13:37.194 --> 00:13:39.108
She's six months today.

00:13:40.273 --> 00:13:43.412
It's big right? Growing like a weed.

00:13:43.447 --> 00:13:45.182
Yeah.

00:13:49.618 --> 00:13:51.624
Monica...

00:13:51.985 --> 00:13:53.750
Yeah?

00:13:55.713 --> 00:13:57.087
Just uh...

00:13:57.122 --> 00:13:58.892
Just take care of yourself, okay?

00:13:58.927 --> 00:14:01.225
Yeah, you too Sam. We'll see you around.

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:01.744
Yeah.

00:14:03.479 --> 00:14:06.077
Oh, here's daddy!

00:15:10.728 --> 00:15:12.453
What are you...?

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:22.760
Rosy?

00:15:29.613 --> 00:15:31.525
No!

00:15:43.364 --> 00:15:45.333
A vision?

00:15:45.368 --> 00:15:47.289
Yes.

00:15:47.481 --> 00:15:50.640
I saw the Demon burning
a woman on the ceiling.

00:15:50.675 --> 00:15:53.107
Right and you think this is gonna
happen to this woman you met because...

00:15:53.142 --> 00:15:56.991
Because these things happen
exactly the way I see them.

00:15:57.026 --> 00:15:58.914
He started them as nightmares and...

00:15:58.949 --> 00:16:01.138
It started when he was awake.

00:16:01.173 --> 00:16:02.970
Yeah.

00:16:03.383 --> 00:16:06.592
It's like... I don't know,
it's like the closer I get...

00:16:06.627 --> 00:16:09.951
To anything involving the Demon
the stronger the visions get.

00:16:09.986 --> 00:16:13.045
All right, when were you
gonna tell me about this?

00:16:14.173 --> 00:16:15.592
We didn't know what it meant.

00:16:15.627 --> 00:16:20.665
All right, something like this starts happening to
your brother you pick up the phone and you call me.

00:16:21.111 --> 00:16:23.002
Call you?

00:16:23.791 --> 00:16:26.016
Are you kidding me?

00:16:26.808 --> 00:16:28.893
Dad, I called you from Lawrence.

00:16:28.928 --> 00:16:31.677
All right, Sam called
you when I was dying.

00:16:31.732 --> 00:16:35.193
I mean, getting you on the phone I got
a better chance winning the lottery.

00:16:40.548 --> 00:16:42.809
You're right.

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:49.420
Although, I'm not crazy about this new
tone of yours, you're right. I'm sorry.

00:16:49.455 --> 00:16:50.875
Look, guys. Visions or no visions.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:54.055
The fact is we know the
Demon is coming tonight.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:57.195
And this family is going through
the same hell that we went through.

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.864
No, they're not.

00:16:58.899 --> 00:17:02.260
No one is. Ever again.

00:17:08.663 --> 00:17:10.318
Hello.

00:17:10.353 --> 00:17:11.973
Sam?

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:13.603
Who is this?

00:17:13.638 --> 00:17:17.784
Think real hard, it'll come to you.

00:17:18.647 --> 00:17:20.478
Meg?

00:17:22.778 --> 00:17:25.061
Last time I saw you,
you fell out of a window.

00:17:25.096 --> 00:17:27.044
Yeah, thanks to you.

00:17:27.079 --> 00:17:29.400
That really hurt my feelings by the way.

00:17:29.435 --> 00:17:31.116
Just your feelings?

00:17:31.151 --> 00:17:33.719
That was a seven story drop.

00:17:33.754 --> 00:17:36.287
Let me speak to your dad.

00:17:38.763 --> 00:17:40.262
My dad?

00:17:40.297 --> 00:17:41.643
I don't know where my dad is.

00:17:41.678 --> 00:17:47.442
It's time for the grown ups to
talk, Sam. Let me speak to him, now.

00:17:56.112 --> 00:17:57.954
This is John.

00:17:57.989 --> 00:18:00.425
Howdy, John? I'm Meg.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:02.827
I'm a friend of your boys.

00:18:02.862 --> 00:18:06.518
I'm also the one who watched Jim
Murphy choke on his own blood.

00:18:09.185 --> 00:18:11.608
Still there, John boy?

00:18:11.643 --> 00:18:12.805
I'm here.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.532
That was yesterday.

00:18:14.533 --> 00:18:17.118
Today I'm in Lincoln.

00:18:18.874 --> 00:18:22.160
Visiting another old friend of yours.

00:18:22.195 --> 00:18:25.175
He wants to say hi.

00:18:25.501 --> 00:18:27.315
John, whatever they do don't...

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.871
Caleb?

00:18:30.088 --> 00:18:32.049
Caleb?

00:18:32.479 --> 00:18:34.143
You listen to me...

00:18:34.178 --> 00:18:37.512
He's got nothing to do with
anything. You let him go.

00:18:37.547 --> 00:18:40.646
We know you have the Colt, John.

00:18:40.988 --> 00:18:43.016
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:18:43.051 --> 00:18:44.732
Oh?

00:18:44.767 --> 00:18:46.414
Okay.

00:18:47.016 --> 00:18:49.581
So, listen to this.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.263
Caleb?

00:18:55.446 --> 00:18:56.509
Caleb?

00:18:56.544 --> 00:18:58.000
You hear that?

00:18:58.035 --> 00:18:59.842
That's the sound of your friend dying.

00:18:59.877 --> 00:19:01.961
Now, let's try this again.

00:19:01.996 --> 00:19:05.295
We know you have the gun,
John. Words travel fast.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:09.367
So as far as we're concerned,
you just declared war.

00:19:09.402 --> 00:19:13.404
And this is what war looks
like. It has casualties.

00:19:14.243 --> 00:19:16.924
I'm gonna kill you, you know that?

00:19:16.959 --> 00:19:18.735
Oh, John. Please.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:20.509
Mind your blood pressure.

00:19:20.544 --> 00:19:22.214
So, this is the thing.

00:19:22.249 --> 00:19:24.927
We're gonna keep doing what we're doing.

00:19:24.962 --> 00:19:26.680
And your friends...

00:19:26.715 --> 00:19:28.644
and anyone who has ever helped you?

00:19:28.679 --> 00:19:33.052
Gave you shelter, anyone you ever loved.

00:19:33.087 --> 00:19:37.426
They'll all die unless
you give us that gun.

00:19:41.119 --> 00:19:46.180
I'm waiting Johny. Better
answer before the buzzer.

00:19:46.633 --> 00:19:48.108
Okay.

00:19:48.143 --> 00:19:51.702
Sorry? I didn't quite get that.

00:19:51.737 --> 00:19:53.380
I said okay.

00:19:53.415 --> 00:19:55.915
I'll bring you the Colt.

00:19:56.246 --> 00:19:58.216
There's a warehouse in Lincoln.

00:19:58.251 --> 00:20:00.726
In the corner of Wellbasher and Lake.

00:20:00.761 --> 00:20:02.531
You're gonna meet me there.

00:20:02.566 --> 00:20:05.233
It's gonna take me about
a day's drive to get there.

00:20:05.268 --> 00:20:07.294
Meet me there at midnight tonight.

00:20:07.329 --> 00:20:08.033
That's impossible.

00:20:08.034 --> 00:20:10.995
I can't get there in time and I
can't just carry a gun on a plane.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:15.007
Oh, then I guess your
friends die, don't they?

00:20:16.005 --> 00:20:18.114
If you do decide to make it...

00:20:18.149 --> 00:20:20.343
Come alone.

00:20:27.541 --> 00:20:30.889
What the hell are you looking at?

00:20:31.341 --> 00:20:33.534
So you think Meg is a demon?

00:20:33.569 --> 00:20:36.163
Either that or she's possessed by one.

00:20:36.198 --> 00:20:37.338
It doesn't really matter.

00:20:37.481 --> 00:20:37.481
What do we do?

00:20:37.516 --> 00:20:39.436
I'm going to Lincoln.

00:20:39.471 --> 00:20:40.353
What?

00:20:40.354 --> 00:20:42.231
Doesn't seem like I have a choice.

00:20:42.266 --> 00:20:45.856
If I don't go, a lot of
people die. Our friends die.

00:20:45.891 --> 00:20:48.133
Dad, the Demon is coming tonight.

00:20:48.168 --> 00:20:50.433
For Monica and her family
that gun is all we've got.

00:20:50.468 --> 00:20:52.238
You can't just hand it over.

00:20:52.273 --> 00:20:54.008
Who said about handing it over?

00:20:54.009 --> 00:20:56.878
Look, besides us and a couple of
vampires no one's really seen the gun.

00:20:56.913 --> 00:20:58.401
No one knows what it looks like.

00:20:58.436 --> 00:21:01.297
So what? You're just gonna
pick up a ringer in a pawn shop?

00:21:01.332 --> 00:21:03.779
Antique store.

00:21:03.987 --> 00:21:06.345
You're gonna hand Meg a fake
gun and hopes she doesn't notice?

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:08.435
Look, as long as it's close...

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:10.169
She shouldn't be able
to tell the difference.

00:21:10.204 --> 00:21:12.922
Yeah, but for how long? What
happens when she figures it out?

00:21:12.957 --> 00:21:14.144
I just...

00:21:14.179 --> 00:21:17.333
I just need to buy a
few hours, that's all.

00:21:17.368 --> 00:21:20.512
You mean for Dean and me?

00:21:22.971 --> 00:21:26.783
You want us to stay here?

00:21:27.451 --> 00:21:29.732
And kill this Demon by ourselves.

00:21:29.767 --> 00:21:32.065
No, Sam.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:34.843
I want to stop losing people we love.

00:21:34.878 --> 00:21:39.608
I want you to go to school I
want... I want Dean to have a home.

00:21:44.109 --> 00:21:47.790
I want Mary alive.

00:21:50.724 --> 00:21:52.831
It's just...

00:21:55.137 --> 00:21:59.046
I just want this to be over.

00:22:31.014 --> 00:22:32.847
Did you get it?

00:22:45.533 --> 00:22:48.168
You know this is a trap, don't you?

00:22:50.104 --> 00:22:51.843
That's why Meg wanted you to come alone.

00:22:51.878 --> 00:22:53.297
I can handle her.

00:22:53.332 --> 00:22:56.311
I have the wholed loaded.
Holy water, mandake, amu...

00:22:56.346 --> 00:22:57.807
Dad.

00:22:57.842 --> 00:22:59.269
What?

00:22:59.765 --> 00:23:01.384
Promise me something.

00:23:01.419 --> 00:23:03.509
What's that?

00:23:03.686 --> 00:23:07.726
If this doesn't go south
just get the hell out.

00:23:07.761 --> 00:23:12.034
Don't get yourself killed, all
right? You're no good to us dead.

00:23:14.741 --> 00:23:17.621
Same goes for you.

00:23:18.697 --> 00:23:21.066
All right, listen to me.

00:23:21.832 --> 00:23:25.409
They made the bullets
special for this Colt.

00:23:25.444 --> 00:23:27.697
Only four of them left.

00:23:27.732 --> 00:23:31.374
Without them, this gun is useless.

00:23:33.059 --> 00:23:35.149
You make every shot count.

00:23:35.184 --> 00:23:36.664
Yes, sir.

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:42.703
I've been waiting a
long time for this fight.

00:23:42.738 --> 00:23:46.956
Now it's here and I'm
not gonna be in it.

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:50.884
It's up to you boys now.

00:23:52.794 --> 00:23:55.339
It's your fight. You finish this.

00:23:55.374 --> 00:23:57.523
You finished what I started.

00:23:57.558 --> 00:23:59.919
You understand?

00:24:20.362 --> 00:24:23.059
We'll see you soon dad.

00:24:27.208 --> 00:24:28.905
I'll see you later.

00:24:53.883 --> 00:24:55.918
Later...

00:26:18.743 --> 00:26:20.894
Maybe we can tell them
there's a gas leak.

00:26:20.929 --> 00:26:23.577
Might get them out of
the house for a few hours.

00:26:23.612 --> 00:26:27.136
How many times did that work for us?

00:26:27.336 --> 00:26:28.887
Yeah.

00:26:32.117 --> 00:26:35.828
Could always tell them the truth.

00:26:37.531 --> 00:26:38.741
Na...

00:26:38.776 --> 00:26:39.952
I know.

00:26:39.953 --> 00:26:43.029
I know, I know, I just...

00:26:43.064 --> 00:26:44.968
What's to become of these people?

00:26:45.003 --> 00:26:47.434
Sam, we only got one move
and you know it, all right?

00:26:47.469 --> 00:26:49.866
We got to wait for that Demon
to show itself and then...

00:26:49.901 --> 00:26:52.912
We get it before it gets them.

00:26:56.870 --> 00:26:59.962
I wonder what dad's doing.

00:27:01.831 --> 00:27:05.803
I would feel a lot better if
we were there backing him up.

00:27:08.090 --> 00:27:12.200
I would feel a lot better
if he was here backing us up.

00:28:48.162 --> 00:28:50.418
This is what we have.

00:28:50.920 --> 00:28:52.740
What?

00:28:53.260 --> 00:28:56.777
After all those years
we're finally here.

00:28:56.812 --> 00:28:59.430
It doesn't seem real.

00:29:00.303 --> 00:29:04.129
We just got to keep our heads
and do our job like always.

00:29:04.164 --> 00:29:07.460
Yeah, but this isn't like always.

00:29:10.241 --> 00:29:12.331
True.

00:29:13.947 --> 00:29:16.272
Dean, uh...

00:29:18.976 --> 00:29:21.418
I want to thank you.

00:29:22.473 --> 00:29:25.047
For what?

00:29:27.105 --> 00:29:29.643
For everything.

00:29:29.678 --> 00:29:31.852
You've always led my back you know.

00:29:31.887 --> 00:29:36.199
Even when I can't count on anyone
I could always count on you.

00:29:36.234 --> 00:29:38.288
And now...

00:29:38.643 --> 00:29:41.341
I don't know, I just
want to let you know.

00:29:41.376 --> 00:29:42.650
Just incase.

00:29:42.685 --> 00:29:45.115
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Are you kidding me?

00:29:45.150 --> 00:29:46.167
What?

00:29:46.202 --> 00:29:48.315
Don't say just incase
something happens to you.

00:29:48.350 --> 00:29:50.429
I don't want to hear
that freaking speech man.

00:29:50.464 --> 00:29:52.615
Nobody is dying tonight.

00:29:52.650 --> 00:29:55.723
Not us, not that family, nobody.

00:29:56.324 --> 00:29:58.575
Except that Demon.

00:29:58.610 --> 00:30:03.502
That evil son of a bitch ain't getting
any older than tonight. You understand me?

00:30:14.757 --> 00:30:16.949
John. You made it.

00:30:16.984 --> 00:30:19.106
Too bad really.

00:30:19.141 --> 00:30:21.569
I was hoping to kill
more of your friends.

00:30:21.604 --> 00:30:23.796
Sorry to disappoint.

00:30:23.831 --> 00:30:27.502
I can see where your
boys get their good looks.

00:30:27.537 --> 00:30:33.570
I must admit, considering what they
say about you I thought you'd be taller.

00:30:36.051 --> 00:30:38.823
Well, aren't you the chatty one?

00:30:38.858 --> 00:30:41.595
You want to get to business?

00:30:42.236 --> 00:30:43.939
Fine.

00:30:44.652 --> 00:30:46.591
Why don't you hand over the gun?

00:30:46.626 --> 00:30:49.593
If I give you the gun,
how do I get out of here?

00:30:49.628 --> 00:30:53.674
If you're as good as they say you are,
I'm sure you'll figure something out.

00:30:53.709 --> 00:30:55.618
Maybe I'll just shoot you.

00:30:55.653 --> 00:30:58.250
You want to shoot me, baby? Go ahead.

00:30:58.285 --> 00:31:03.327
It won't end anything.
There's more where I came from.

00:31:07.495 --> 00:31:09.061
Who the hell's that?

00:31:09.096 --> 00:31:13.435
He's not as nearly as much fun
as I am, I can tell you that.

00:31:13.470 --> 00:31:17.286
So, I suggest you give us the gun.

00:31:23.449 --> 00:31:25.786
Now!

00:31:36.044 --> 00:31:38.232
This is the Colt?

00:31:43.736 --> 00:31:46.272
What do you think?

00:32:07.569 --> 00:32:09.922
You shot me!

00:32:10.506 --> 00:32:14.089
I can't believe you just shot me!

00:32:15.321 --> 00:32:17.609
It's a fake!

00:32:27.475 --> 00:32:28.982
You're dead John.

00:32:29.017 --> 00:32:30.455
You're boys are dead.

00:32:30.490 --> 00:32:33.466
I never used the gun. How can
I know it would never work?

00:32:33.501 --> 00:32:36.443
I'm so not in the mood for
this. I've just been shot!

00:32:36.478 --> 00:32:39.371
Well I guess you're
lucky the gun wasn't real.

00:32:39.406 --> 00:32:41.164
That's funny, John.

00:32:41.199 --> 00:32:46.603
We're gonna strip the skin from
your bones but that was funny.

00:33:31.008 --> 00:33:33.561
Holy water, John.

00:33:33.596 --> 00:33:36.457
Real cute.

00:33:46.660 --> 00:33:49.241
Dad's not answering.

00:33:52.216 --> 00:33:54.133
Maybe Meg was late.

00:33:54.168 --> 00:33:55.756
Maybe the reception is bad.

00:33:55.791 --> 00:33:57.098
Yeah, well...

00:34:02.513 --> 00:34:04.715
Dean, wait.

00:34:05.599 --> 00:34:07.281
Listen.

00:34:30.309 --> 00:34:32.451
It's coming.

00:34:40.279 --> 00:34:41.832
Damn it.

00:35:09.769 --> 00:35:11.502
Get out of my house!

00:35:12.788 --> 00:35:14.522
Get out of my house!

00:35:16.482 --> 00:35:17.561
Mr. Hold, please.

00:35:17.596 --> 00:35:18.493
Be quite and listen to me.

00:35:18.494 --> 00:35:20.710
Be quite and listen to me.
We are trying to help you.

00:35:20.745 --> 00:35:21.714
Charlie?

00:35:21.749 --> 00:35:22.683
Okay?

00:35:22.684 --> 00:35:23.821
Everything okay down there?

00:35:23.856 --> 00:35:24.830
Monica, get the baby!

00:35:24.831 --> 00:35:26.007
Don't go over there!

00:35:26.042 --> 00:35:27.183
You stay away from her!

00:35:33.213 --> 00:35:35.559
What are you..

00:35:50.325 --> 00:35:51.758
Where the hell did it go?

00:35:51.793 --> 00:35:52.293
My baby!

00:35:52.328 --> 00:35:53.800
No, hey wait.

00:35:53.801 --> 00:35:55.740
Get her out of here, I got it.

00:35:56.010 --> 00:35:57.219
Come on.

00:35:57.254 --> 00:35:58.213
My baby!

00:35:58.248 --> 00:35:59.279
Dean's got her.

00:36:55.638 --> 00:36:57.623
You get away from my family!

00:36:57.658 --> 00:36:59.608
Charlie, don't. They saved us.

00:36:59.643 --> 00:37:01.255
They saved us...

00:37:09.130 --> 00:37:10.981
Thank you.

00:37:15.067 --> 00:37:16.733
It's still in there.

00:37:17.013 --> 00:37:18.128
Sam, Sam. No!

00:37:18.163 --> 00:37:19.504
Dean, let me go. It's still in there!

00:37:19.539 --> 00:37:20.845
It's burning to the
ground. It's suicide!

00:37:20.880 --> 00:37:21.714
I don't care!

00:37:21.749 --> 00:37:23.043
I do!

00:37:39.027 --> 00:37:42.889
Come on, dad. Answer
your phone, damn it!

00:37:46.494 --> 00:37:48.989
Something's wrong.

00:37:51.094 --> 00:37:53.266
You hear me? Something's happened.

00:37:53.301 --> 00:37:55.438
If you had just let me go in there...

00:37:55.473 --> 00:37:58.678
I could have ended all this.

00:37:58.713 --> 00:38:00.092
Sam...

00:38:00.127 --> 00:38:03.227
The only thing you
would end was your life.

00:38:03.905 --> 00:38:06.262
You don't know that.

00:38:06.297 --> 00:38:09.914
So what? You're willing to
sacrifice yourself? Is that it?

00:38:10.423 --> 00:38:12.665
Yeah. Yeah, you're damn right I am.

00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:14.907
Yeah, well that's not gonna
happen. Not as long as I'm around.

00:38:14.942 --> 00:38:16.451
What the hell are you
talking about Dean?

00:38:16.486 --> 00:38:19.217
We've been searching for
this Demon our whole lives.

00:38:19.252 --> 00:38:20.858
It's the only thing
we've ever cared about.

00:38:20.893 --> 00:38:23.667
Sam, I want to waste it. I do, okay?

00:38:23.702 --> 00:38:25.661
But it's not worth dying over?

00:38:25.696 --> 00:38:26.215
What?

00:38:26.250 --> 00:38:27.565
I mean it.

00:38:27.566 --> 00:38:31.035
If hunting this Demon means
you getting yourself killed.

00:38:31.070 --> 00:38:33.417
Then I hope we never
find the damn thing.

00:38:33.452 --> 00:38:36.433
That thing killed Jess.

00:38:37.335 --> 00:38:40.095
That thing killed mom.

00:38:40.563 --> 00:38:43.478
You said yourself once.

00:38:43.629 --> 00:38:46.621
That no matter what we do they're gone

00:38:46.656 --> 00:38:49.063
and they're never coming back.

00:38:49.521 --> 00:38:52.284
Don't just say that! Don't you!

00:38:52.319 --> 00:38:55.047
After all this, don't you say that.

00:38:56.629 --> 00:39:00.230
Sam, look.

00:39:00.265 --> 00:39:03.082
The three of us...

00:39:03.285 --> 00:39:06.081
That's all we have.

00:39:07.587 --> 00:39:10.611
It's all I have.

00:39:13.834 --> 00:39:18.092
Sometimes I feel like I'm
barely holding it together, man.

00:39:18.954 --> 00:39:21.846
Without you and dad...

00:39:22.820 --> 00:39:24.889
Dad...

00:39:29.975 --> 00:39:32.351
He should have called by now.

00:39:32.386 --> 00:39:34.851
Try again.

00:39:51.377 --> 00:39:55.189
You boys really screwed up this time.

00:39:58.058 --> 00:40:00.408
Where is he?

00:40:00.588 --> 00:40:03.840
You're never gonna
see your father again.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
